# 11. YARA Detection

**YARA** is a pattern-matching tool commonly used to identify suspicious files or content based on defined rules.

A YARA rule can be created to detect characteristics associated with CVE-2024-21413 exploitation.

One important characteristic is the presence of:

```text
file://
```

combined with other suspicious characteristics of a crafted Moniker Link.

Conceptually:

```text
Email
   |
   v
YARA Rule
   |
   v
Pattern Matching
   |
   +---- Suspicious Pattern Found
   |             |
   |             v
   |       Potential Malicious Email
   |
   +---- No Match
```

YARA is a **detection mechanism**, not an exploitation tool.

