# 12. Network Analysis with Wireshark

**Wireshark** can be used to inspect network packets generated during the interaction.

In the lab, network traffic associated with the SMB authentication attempt can be observed using Wireshark.

Simplified flow:

```text
Victim System
     |
     v
SMB Authentication Request
     |
     v
Network Packets
     |
     v
Wireshark
     |
     v
Packet Analysis
```

The packet capture can reveal information associated with the NTLM authentication exchange.

This demonstrates how network monitoring tools can help security analysts investigate suspicious authentication activity.

